Outer-fold test accuracy on Iris (OpenML 61) over 10$\times$ stratified 5-fold cross-validation (50 folds). (a) Each dot is one outer fold (jittered horizontally; accuracies move in steps of 1/30); diamonds and bars are the mean and the 95\% corrected resampled-$t$ interval (Nadeau \& Bengio, 2003). (b) Paired fold-wise difference, logistic regression $-$ kNN, in percentage points, with the same interval; the dashed line is zero. Intervals are not clipped at 100\%.
